Track 2: Don Pedro’s Invisible Chalk
- Story & Context: Named after the legendary surveyor who wandered three levels down without a flashlight, this confession piece was captured on a 4-track cassette recorder using a solitary contact mic affixed to a structural spruce timber. Between the mournful, bowed groans of the upright bass, you can hear the faint click of buttons as Valeria translated her uncle's descent into frantic, 8-bit arpeggios that mimic a playground game of hopscotch played in pitch darkness. Halfway through the drone, guest singer Rosa Cayo whispers into a cavern echo: "Step only on the squares that do not sing back."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Surrealist digital art of an endless, damp underground tunnel where glowing pixelated hopscotch squares stretch out along the dirt floor, disappearing into deep chthonic mist.

