- Story & Context: The final mythic track documents the aftermath of the 2021 shaft collapse at Cerro Verde, which swallowed three ventilation shafts and turned the entire mountain into a massive natural acoustic resonator. Using samples of air rushing through fractured zinc tubing mixed with a triumphant, swirling Farfisa lead, the song celebrates survival through pure, stumbling rhythm. Tadeo’s bass walks a manic, swinging line under crushed square-wave chirps as the full chorus roars from the mouth of the tunnel: "The mountain ate our lead, but she spit out the melody."
